1. Open your Linux terminal and use the pwd, ls, and cd commands to navigate to your Downloads folder and list all files inside it.
=>pwd
ls
cd ~/Downloads
ls -la

2. Create a new directory called 'music_playlist' inside your home directory using the mkdir command, then use the touch command to create three empty files named song1.mp3, song2.mp3, and song3.mp3 inside it.
=>mkdir ~/music_playlist
cd ~/music_playlist
touch song1.mp3 song2.mp3 song3.mp3
ls

3. Use the cp command to copy all files from your 'music_playlist' directory to a new directory called 'backup_playlist', then use the ls command to verify the files were copied.
=>mkdir ~/backup_playlist
cp ~/music_playlist/* ~/backup_playlist/
ls ~/backup_playlist

4. Use the mv command to rename 'song1.mp3' to 'favorite_song.mp3' inside the 'music_playlist' directory, and then use the rm command to delete 'song3.mp3' from the same directory.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Make sure you are inside the correct directory before running mv or rm.</em>
=>cd ~/music_playlist
mv song1.mp3 favorite_song.mp3
rm song3.mp3
ls
